['The task you've mentioned is a complex one and involves several distinct components that require careful design. The code here will serve as a basic blueprint for creating such a system. This doesn't include all the features you described due to the complexity of implementing those in Java, but it should give you a starting point.

```java
import java.util.*;

public class DistributedHashTable {
    private int capacity;
    private int replicationFactor;
    private List<Node> nodes = new ArrayList<>();

    public DistributedHashTable(int capacity, int replicationFactor) throws IllegalArgumentException {
        if (capacity <= 0 || replicationFactor <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Capacity and Replication Factor must be greater than 0");

        this.capacity = capacity;
        this.replicationFactor = replicationFactor;
    }

    public void addNode(String nodeId, String ipAddress, int port) {
        Node newNode = new Node(nodeId, ipAddress, port);

        if (nodes.size() >= capacity) throw new RuntimeException("DHT is at maximum capacity");

        nodes.add(newNode);
    }

    public void put(String key, String value, ConsistentHashing hashFunction) {
        int primaryNodeIndex = hashFunction.hash(key);

        Node primaryNode = nodes.get(primaryNodeIndex % capacity);

        for (int i = 1; i < replicationFactor; ++i) {
            int replicaNodeIndex = (primaryNodeIndex + i * i) % capacity;

            Node replicaNode = nodes.get(replicaNodeIndex);

            primaryNode.putReplica(key, value, replicaNode);
        }

        primaryNode.putPrimary(key, value);
    }

    public String get(String key) {
        int nodeIndex = consistentHashing(key);

        Node node = nodes.get(nodeIndex % capacity);

        return node.getValue(key);
    }
}

class Node {
    private String id;
    private Map<String, String> data = new HashMap<>();

    public Node(String id, String ipAddress, int port) {
        this.id = id;

        //initialize IP and Port for the node
    }

    public void putPrimary(String key, String value) {
        data.put(key, value);
    }

    public void putReplica(String key, String value, Node replicaNode) {
        replicaNode.data.put(key, value);
    }

    public String getValue(String key) {
        return data.getOrDefault(key, null);
    }
}
```
Please note that this is a simplified and basic version of what you're asking for. There are many aspects that should be considered in detail including error handling, logging, network communication, load balancing strategies, consistent hashing, memory management etc.,  and these were not included due to the complexity. 

For a full-featured distributed system like this one, you would likely use an existing library or framework which is designed for that purpose such as Apache Hadoop's Distributed Hash Table (DHT) implementation or Hazelcast.
