    printf("Number of contexts: %zu\n", array->size);
}
```
This approach has the advantage of being simple and easy to understand, but may not be suitable for systems where detailed monitoring is required. In such cases, a more sophisticated logging strategy with different levels of detail (e.g., debug, info, warning, error) and customizable output formats could be used.

