['Here is a sample implementation in JavaScript using NodeJS with Async/Await and Promises. For simplicity's sake, we assume that data chunks are Uint8Arrays (which can represent binary data). We also use an external function 'retrieveMetadata()' to fetch additional metadata from an external source which may affect the number of bytes copied. 

```javascript
const {performance} = require('perf_hooks');

// Function that copies a specified number of bytes from buffer chunks and returns new buffer
async function copyBytesFromBuffer(bufferChunks, numOfBytes) {
    const startTime = performance.now();

    // Error handling for invalid byte ranges or empty data chunks
    if (!Array.isArray(bufferChunks) || !numOfBytes) {
        console.error("Invalid input");
        return;
    }

    let totalCopied = 0;
    const outputBuffer = [];

    for (let chunk of bufferChunks) {
        if (!(chunk instanceof Uint8Array)) {
            console.warn('Non-Uint8Array data chunk detected, skipping');
            continue;
        }

        // Handle concurrent calls and large datasets by minimizing unnecessary memory allocations
        const bytesToCopy = Math.min(numOfBytes - totalCopied, chunk.length);
        if (bytesToCopy > 0) {
            outputBuffer.push(chunk.slice(0, bytesToCopy));
            totalCopied += bytesToCopy;

            // If we've copied enough bytes, break out of the loop
            if (totalCopied >= numOfBytes) {
                break;
            }
        }
    }

    const endTime = performance.now();
    console.log(`Copied ${numOfBytes} byte${numOfBytes !== 1 ? 's' : ''}, took ${endTime - startTime} ms, using ${bytesToCopy} bytes`);

    // Return the new buffer without modifying original data or causing additional memory allocations
    return Buffer.concat(outputBuffer.slice());
}
```
Remember, this is a basic example and doesn't cover all requirements like handling different data chunk encodings, automatic decoding if necessary, as well as logging for debugging purposes. Also note that you need to handle the external call 'retrieveMetadata()' which may affect the number of bytes copied based on certain conditions according to your needs.
