['Here is a basic implementation of the described function in PHP. Please note that this is a simplified example and does not cover all of your specifications due to complexity but it can serve as a starting point:

```php
function secureHashAndRandom($length, $algorithm = 'bcrypt') {
    // Initialize an array for supported algorithms
    $supportedAlgorithms = ['bcrypt', 'argon2', 'pbkdf2'];

    // Verify the chosen algorithm is supported
    if (!in_array(strtolower($algorithm), $supportedAlgorithms)) {
        throw new Exception("Unsupported hashing algorithm.");
    }

    // Initialize a string of all possible characters to use for random generation
    $characters = '0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ+*~#@^|%{}[]?><,.;:/';

    // Generate a random string of the specified length using PHP's cryptographically secure method
    $randomString = '';
    for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
        $index = random_int(0, strlen($characters) - 1);
        $randomString .= $characters[$index];
    }

    // Hash the password using the chosen algorithm
    $hashedPassword = '';
    switch (strtolower($algorithm)) {
        case 'bcrypt':
            $hashedPassword = password_hash($randomString, PASSWORD_BCRYPT);
            break;
        case 'argon2i':
            $hashedPassword = password_hash($randomString, PASSWORD_ARGON2I);
            break;
        case 'pbkdf2':
            $hashedPassword = password_hash($randomString, PASSWORD_PBKDF2);
            break;
    }

    // Return the hashed password and the random string
    return [
        "password" => $hashedPassword, 
        "string" => $randomString
    ];
}
```
This function will generate a secure random string of specified length and then hash it using one of the selected algorithms. It uses PHP's `random_int` method to ensure that the generated string is cryptographically secure. However, please note this does not cover all aspects of your specifications due to complexity. For a more robust solution you might want to consider other libraries or modules for these tasks such as Sodium, libsodium-php etc., and proper error handling and logging mechanisms.
