public class LargeTextLogProcessor {
    private LRUMap<String, String> cache = new LRUMap<>(100); // use a suitable size for your application

    public void processFile(Path path) throws IOException {
        try (ZipInputStream zipInput = new ZipInputStream(new BufferedInputStream(Files.newInputStream(path)))) {
            InputStreamReader reader = null;

            if ((reader = new InputStreamReader(zipInput, "UTF-8")) == null) {
                System.err.println("Error: Failed to read the file");
                return;
            }

            BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(reader);
            String line;

            while ((line = in.readLine()) != null) {
                if (cache.containsKey(line)) { // if we have seen this log entry before, use the cache
                    System.out.println("Cached: " + cache.get(line));
                } else { // parse and add to cache for future requests
                    String processedLine = processLogEntry(line);
                    cache.put(line, processedLine);
                    System.out.println("Processed: " + processedLine);
                }
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.err.format("IOException: %s%n", e);
        }
    }

    private String processLogEntry(String logEntry) { // Replace with your parsing logic
        return logEntry; 
    }
}
```
This code uses the Java NIO package to read from a compressed file. We use a LRUMap cache (from Apache Commons Collections) for storing recently accessed logs entries, reducing redundant work and improving performance on frequent lookups. Buffering is used to minimize I/O operations. 

