                $sql = "UPDATE clinics SET status=?, last_modified_ip=?, last_modified_date=? WHERE clinic_id=?";

                if($stmt = $this->db->prepare($sql)){
                    $stmt->bind_param('sssi', $status, $ip, $date, $id);
                    $stmt->execute();
                    // Notify third party API about the status change
                    $this->notifyAPI("Clinic ID: ".$id.", New Status: ".$status);
                } else {
                    $this->logError($this->db->error);
                    throw new Exception('Failed to prepare SQL statement.');
                }
                $stmt->close();
            }
            $this->db->commit();
            return 'Successfully updated clinic statuses';
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            $this->db->rollback();
            $this->logError($e->getMessage());
            throw $e;
        }
    }

    // Verify if a clinic exists in the database
    private function verifyClinicExist($id) {
        $sql = "SELECT 1 FROM clinics WHERE clinic_id=?";
        $stmt = $this->db->prepare($sql);
        if ($stmt) $stmt->bind_param('i', $id);
        $stmt->execute();
        $result = $stmt->get_result()->num_rows > 0 ? true : false;
        $stmt->close();
        return $result;
    }

    // Notify the third party API about clinic status change
    private function notifyAPI($message) {
        // Replace with actual HTTP request to external API
        $this->logError("External API notification: ".$message);
    }

    // Log any errors that occur during the execution
    private function logError($errorMessage) {
        error_log('Error: '.$errorMessage, 0);
    }
}
?>
```
This PHP script uses object-oriented programming principles to encapsulate all related functions and database connections within a class. The updateStatusBatch method accepts an associative array of clinic IDs and their new statuses, updates the database in a transaction for concurrency control, logs any errors that occur during the execution, and notifies a third party API about each successful status change. 

The verifyClinicExist function ensures that the clinic ID exists before attempting to update it. If a clinic does not exist, the script will continue with the next clinic ID in the array without throwing an error or stopping execution. The notifyAPI method represents a placeholder for integrating with an external API and currently just logs the message as a string, but this could be replaced with actual HTTP requests to call out to an external service. 

