['Here is an example implementation using Java's `ConcurrentHashMap` for storing sessions in a thread-safe manner:

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.logging.*;

public class SessionManager {
    private static final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(SessionManager.class.getName());

    // Sessions map with user ID as key and session as value
    private ConcurrentHashMap<String, UserSession> sessions = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    private ScheduledExecutorService executor;
    private long expiryPeriodMillis;

    public SessionManager(long expiryPeriodMillis) {
        this.expiryPeriodMillis = expiryPeriodMillis;

        // Start an executor to periodically check and remove sessions
        this.executor = Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor();
        this.executor.scheduleWithFixedDelay(this::cleanupExpiredSessions, 1, expiryPeriodMillis / 2, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
    }

    // Add new session or update existing one
    public void putSession(String userId, UserProfile profile) {
        UserSession session = sessions.get(userId);

        if (session == null) {
            session = new UserSession();
            sessions.put(userId, session);

            logger.info("Created session for " + userId);
        } else {
            // Handle concurrent updates gracefully
            synchronized (session) {
                session.getProfile().updateFrom(profile);

                // Log update operation
                logger.info("Updated profile for " + userId);
            }
        }
    }

    private void cleanupExpiredSessions() {
        long currentTime = System.currentTimeMillis();

        sessions.entrySet().removeIf(entry -> {
            UserSession session = entry.getValue();

            synchronized (session) {
                if ((currentTime - session.getLastActivityTime()) > expiryPeriodMillis) {
                    logger.info("Removed session for " + entry.getKey());

                    // Release resources
                    session.releaseResources();

                    return true;
                }

                return false;
            }
        });
    }

    public void shutdown() {
        executor.shutdownNow();

        sessions.values().forEach(UserSession::releaseResources);
        sessions = null;
    }
}
```

Please note that this example is quite simplified and may need further refinement depending on the specific requirements of your application. For instance, `UserProfile` and `UserSession` classes are not provided but should be defined according to the needs of your application. Also, the logging mechanism and error handling is kept minimalistic for brevity.
']

