```javascript
const dynamicLoad = (filesToLoad) => {
    let promises = filesToLoad.map(filePath => new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        const scriptTag = document.createElement('script');
        scriptTag.src = filePath;

        scriptTag.onload = () => resolve();
        scriptTag.onerror = (err) => reject(new Error(`Failed to load ${filePath} because of: ${err}`));

        document.head.appendChild(scriptTag);
    }));

  return Promise.allSettled(promises).then((results) => 
      results.forEach(result => console.log('File', result.status === 'fulfilled' ? 'loaded successfully.' : `loading failed: ${result.reason}`))
  );
};
```
This is a basic function that loads multiple JavaScript files dynamically into the webpage context by appending script tags to the head of the document. It creates a new promise for each file and resolves or rejects it based on whether the script was successfully loaded or not. The Promise.allSettled ensures all promises are resolved regardless of their outcome, then logs the status of each one.

